LOCAL PATCH (not submitted anywhere): phy: hisilicon: histb-combphy — SATA-mode nano tuning

histb_combphy_init() writes the vendor's PCIe tuning (nano[0x1]=0x8, [0xc]=0x9, [0x1a]=0x4) in
every mode. On the HiMedia Q10 Pro (Hi3798CV200, combphy1 in SATA mode) that leaves the SATA
receiver marginal: 10B8B/BadCRC on an idle link (4-33 error-seconds a minute), and under a 2 GB
read 6 exceptions + 6 hard resets + a drop to UDMA/100. The vendor SATA driver (hiahci-phy, stock
3.18) writes nano[0x1]=0x4 only; with it: 0 error-seconds, and 2 GB reads + a 1 GB rewrite with
CRC +0 / 0 resets. A sweep of nano[0x1]: 2, 4, 6 clean, bit 3 set errs.

The value has to be in place before the first link training. Applying it from userspace after
the driver trained the link blips the PHY (PHYRdyChg), and with root I/O in flight libata's
recovery failed (IDENTIFY timeouts, device disabled, ext4 journal aborted).
docs/261014-himedia-sata-kernel-vs-board.md

--- a/drivers/phy/hisilicon/phy-histb-combphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/hisilicon/phy-histb-combphy.c
@@ -131,6 +131,20 @@
 
 	/* Need to wait for EP clock stable */
 	mdelay(5);
+
+	/*
+	 * LOCAL (HiMedia Q10 Pro / Hi3798CV200): the values below are the vendor's PCIe tuning
+	 * (Poplar). In SATA mode nano[0x1] = 0x8 leaves the receiver marginal: 10B8B/BadCRC on an
+	 * idle link, hard resets and UDMA/100 under load (measured 2026-10-14). The vendor SATA
+	 * driver (hiahci-phy) writes nano[0x1] = 0x4 and nothing else here; with it the link is
+	 * clean. It must be set HERE, before the first link training: retuning a live link blips
+	 * the PHY, and under root I/O that wedged the disk.
+	 */
+	if (priv->mode.select == PHY_TYPE_SATA) {
+		nano_register_write(priv, 0x1, 0x4);
+		dev_info(&phy->dev, "SATA mode: nano[0x1] = 0x4 (vendor SATA tuning)\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	/* Configure nano phy registers as suggested by vendor */
 	nano_register_write(priv, 0x1, 0x8);
